orsett Hospitality International (DHI) owns and/or manages a total of over 51 hotels of various brands in major cities around the world together with its sister companies - Malaysia Land Properties Sdn Bhd (Mayland), AGORA Hospitality Group and Palasino Group. Below is a list a properties which are either owned and/or managed by DHI and its business counterparts.\n\n  * Image: Dorsett Residences Bukit Bintang\n\n#### Dorsett Residences Bukit Bintang\n\nIt doesn’t get more central than Dorsett Residences Bukit Bintang. Located steps away from premier shopping and entertainment hubs like Pavilion and Starhill Gallery, our 52 stylish suites and two-bedroom residences offer the perfect stay for families looking for comfort and convenience in the heart of the city.\n\n    * 172, Jalan Imbi, 55100 Kuala Lumpur.\n\nVisit Website\n\n  * Image: Cosmo Hotel Kuala Lumpur\n\n#### Cosmo Hotel Kuala Lumpur\n\nLocated on Leboh Ampang, Cosmo Hotel Kuala Lumpur offers 347 thoughtfully designed guestrooms and suites, blending contemporary comfort with city charm.\n\n    * No.2, Jalan Anjung Putra, Off Jalan Sultan Ismail 50480 Kuala Lumpur\n\nVisit Website\n\n  * Image: Damas Suites & Residences, Kuala Lumpur\n\n#### Damas Suites & Residences, Kuala Lumpur\n\nLocated in Sri Hartamas, just next to Kuala Lumpur’s Royal Palace, our serviced apartments and suites range from 49 to 94 square metres—ideal for guests or families who need a little extra space.\nSri Hartamas is an exclusive enclave, just 10–15 minutes by car from the city centre and only 5 minutes from the Malaysia International Trade and Exhibition Centre (MiTEC). Surrounded by a hip, chic, and trendy atmosphere, our property offers a stylish and convenient base for exploring Kuala Lumpur.\n\n    * Damas Club, Plaza Damas 3, No. 63 Jalan Sri Hartamas 1, Sri Hartamas, 50480 Kuala Lumpur\n\nVisit Website\n\n  * Image: Regalia Suites Kuala Lumpur\n\n#### Regalia Suites Kuala Lumpur\n\nRegalia Suites Kuala Lumpur is a luxury serviced residence, recognised as one of the city’s iconic high-rise landmarks.\nLocated within Kuala Lumpur city centre, the residences are just minutes from Putra World Trade Centre (PWTC) and Sunway Putra Mall. The property is easily accessible via Jalan Kuching, Jalan Sultan Ismail, and Jalan Putra.\nWith Putra Komuter Station, PWTC LRT, and Sultan Ismail LRT all within walking distance, Regalia Suites offers a convenient base to explore the city, with excellent public transport links making travel around Kuala Lumpur a breeze.\n\n    * No. 2, Jalan Anjung Putra,  Off Jalan Sultan Ismail 50480 Kuala Lumpur\n\nVisit Website--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDorsett Residences Sri Hartamas Condominium (Service Residence) 1 Bedroom - 2 Bedroom for sale | StarProperty (https://www.starproperty.my/kuala-lumpur/sri-hartamas/dorsett-residences-sri-hartamas/to-buy/property/9088)\nciteturn370search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.6 years ago; Condominium (Service Residence) ... Mayland Universal Sdn Bhd ... 707 Units ... Dorsett Residences Sri Hartamas is a freehold 700 chicly designed service apartment units under the same roof as Dorsett Hotel in Sri Hartamas.\n\n# Dorsett Residences Sri Hartamas\n\nSri Hartamas\n\nstarting from RM 520,000\n\nfrom\n\nRM 2,101.53\n\nper month *\n\n* This is an indication only. For the exact amount, please check with the bank\n\nCondominium (Service Residence)\n\nFreehold\n\nF/H\n\n1 Bathroom - 1 Bathroom\n\n1 Bedroom - 2 Bedroom\n\n474 sq ft - 1378 sq ft\n\nSales Gallery Location\n\nKL City Centre, Kuala Lumpur\nView map\n\nDeveloper\n\nMayland Universal Sdn Bhd\n\nNumber of units\n\n707 Units\n\nEstimated Completion Date\n\nJune 2019\n\n#### More about Dorsett Residences Sri Hartamas\n\nDorsett Residences Sri Hartamas is a freehold 700 chicly designed service apartment units under the same roof as Dorsett Hotel in Sri Hartamas. The residents will have the hotel services and facilities available to them.\n\nIt is strategically located in the affluent neighbourhoods of Mont Kiara, Hartamas, Damansara Heights and Bangsar. Its connectivity is conveniently linked between KL City Centre, TTDI, Bandar Utama and Mutiara Damansara to Dorsett Residences Sri Hartamas.\n\nThe ease of getting in and out of the area is a breeze with NKVE, Sprint Highways Penchala Link, Kerinchi Link, Duke and roads to other access points around the development. The prestige of the location is further boosted by the presence of the Royal Palace which is less than 500m away from the development.\n\nDorsett Residences Sri Hartamas sits centrally with amenities within walking distance and also within minutes of driving out.\n\nCompletion Year - 2018\n\n#### Additional Feature\n\n24-hr Security\n\nF&B Outlets\n\nGym\n\nFitness Centre\n\nJacuzzi\n\nLounge\n\nMultipurpose Hall\n\nSwimming Pool\n\nSpa\n\n#### Unit Layout\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\nImage\n\n#### Virtual Showroom\n\niframe\n\niframe\n\n#### Location Insights--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMAYLAND UNIVERSAL SDN BHD v. KONG AIK WENG & ORS (https://www.elaw.my/JE/01/JE_2026_39.html)\nciteturn370search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last week; ### MAYLAND UNIVERSAL SDN BHD v. ... The appellant was the developer of a service apartment known as 'Residensi Dorsett Sri Hartamas'. ... [3] The appellant is the developer of a service apartment in a development known as \"Residensi Dorsett Sri Hartamas\".\n\nThe appellant was the developer of a service apartment known as 'Residensi Dorsett Sri Hartamas'. The respondents were purchasers of units in that development and had respectively entered into sale and purchase agreements (\"SPA\") governed by the Housing Development (Control and Licensing) Act 1966 and Schedule H of the Housing Development (Control and Licensing) Regulations 1989. Clause 25(1) of the SPAs required the appellant to deliver vacant possession within 36 months from the date of the SPAs, failing which liquidated damages were payable under cl 25(2). Clause 27(1) prescribed the manner of delivery, including issuance of the separate strata title by the appropriate authority, and cl 28(1) permitted the appellant, notwithstanding cl 27(1)(b), to obtain the Controller's written certification to deliver vacant possession within the time stipulated for the handing over of vacant possession under cl 25(1) if the separate strata title was not issued for any reason not attributable to the appellant. In or around August 2018 the appellant applied to the Controller for such certification, and on 25 January 2019 the Controller granted conditional approval permitting delivery of vacant possession of the respondents' units without the strata titles. Salient Background Facts\n\n[3] The appellant is the developer of a service apartment in a development known as \"Residensi Dorsett Sri Hartamas\". The respondents are the respective purchasers of the service apartment units in the development. The appellant, as the vendor, and the respondents, as the purchasers, had respectively entered into a Sale and Purchase Agreement (hereafter \"the SPA\"). The respective SPAs were governed under the Housing Development (Control and Licensing) Act 1966 and Schedule H of the Housing Development (Control and Licensing) Regulations 1989.\n\n[4] The contractual time frame for delivery of vacant possession of the respective respondents' units was thirty-six (36) months from the respective dates of the SPAs. This is stated in cl 25 of the SPA, which is reproduced below:\n\n> \"Time for delivery of vacant possession\n> \n> 25. (1) Vacant possession of the said Parcel shall be delivered to the Purchaser in the manner stipulated in cl 27 within thirty [sic] (36) months from the date of this Agreement.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDorsett Residences @ Sri Ha